SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Rostarr: Evolving Landscapes
LOCATION:Desa Potato Head
DESCRIPTION:On Friday\, 16 October 2026\, Desa Potato Head will unveil Evol
 ving Landscapes\, the third chapter of its Cultural Exchange Series and Ko
 rean-American artist Rostarr’s largest\, most intricate work yet. The pr
 ogramme will bring together art\, Balinese ritual\, music\, projection map
 ping and fashion across Potato Head Beach Club & Klymax Discotheque. Creat
 ed entirely freehand without stencils\, Evolving Landscapes draws on Rosta
 rr’s signature Graphysics visual language\, combining the discipline of 
 East Asian calligraphy with bold geometric forms. A self-guided digital to
 ur invites visitors to explore individual glyphs and details\, accompanied
  by Rostarr’s memories\, references and observations behind the 1\,644 m
 ² façade. The event also features an on-site pop-up for a capsule collec
 tion made with Japanese label nonnative \, which showcases the label’s u
 tilitarian aesthetic incorporating Evolving Landscapes’ monochrome motif
 s. Doors open at 3 PM \, when Potato Head Beach Club becomes an open-air d
 ancefloor. Archie\, Ryosuke Fukunaga\, Yuka Mizuhara\, Eric Duncan\, Alex 
 From Tokyo and Suze Ijó will take turns behind a Rostarr hand-painted DJ 
 booth until midnight. At 5.30 PM \, the conversation moves to Klymax for D
 esa Dialogues\, where Rostarr and Daniel Mitchell \, Creative Director of 
 Potato Head and founder of Space Available \, will discuss their 17-year c
 reative relationship and the journey from the Green Bus.\n\nMore info: htt
 ps://www.nowbali.co.id/upcoming-events/rostarr-evolving-landscapes/\n\nPle
 ase verify with the organizer before attending.
URL:https://www.nowbali.co.id/upcoming-events/rostarr-evolving-landscapes/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
END:VEVENT
